  "feesApplyText": "<p>For properties in England, in accordance with the Tenant Fees Act 2019, as well as paying the rent, you may also be required to make the following permitted payments payable to <strong>Sterling Sales and Lettings</strong> ( The Agent ):</p><p><strong>Permitted Payments (Assured Periodic Tenancies)</strong></p><p><strong>Holding Deposit</strong>: Maximum of <strong>1 week s rent</strong>. (Reserves the property while reference checks are conducted, subject to statutory terms regarding retention/refund).</p><p><strong>Security Deposit:</strong></p><p>Maximum of <strong>5 weeks  rent</strong> (where annual rent is under \u00a350,000).</p><p>Maximum of <strong>6 weeks  rent</strong> (where annual rent is \u00a350,000 or above).</p><p><strong>During the tenancy (payable to the Agent if applicable):</strong></p><p><strong>Changes/Variations to the Tenancy Agreement</strong>: Capped at <strong>\u00a350 inc. VAT</strong> (or reasonable costs incurred if higher) per agreed variation requested by the tenant.</p><p><strong>Unpaid / Late Rent Interest</strong>: Interest charged at <strong>3% above the Bank of England base rate</strong> calculated from the rent due date once rent is overdue by more than 14 days.</p><p><strong>Lost Keys or Security Devices</strong>: Reasonable costs actually incurred for replacing lost keys or security devices, including lock replacements where necessary.</p><p><strong>Early Termination / Surrender at Tenant s Request</strong>: Should the tenant request to terminate early and the landlord agrees, the tenant remains liable for the rent until a replacement tenant takes occupation, as well as the landlord s reasonably incurred costs in re-letting the property.</p><p><strong>During the tenancy (payable directly to the provider, where applicable)</strong>:</p><p><strong>Utilities</strong>: Electricity, Gas or other fuel, Water, Sewerage.</p><p><strong>Communications</strong>: Telephone, Broadband, Cable or Satellite television installation and subscriptions.</p><p><strong>Television Licence</strong>.</p><p><strong>Council Tax</strong> (payable to the local billing authority).</p><p><strong>Contractual Damages</strong>: Any other permitted payments or damages in the event of default under the terms of the tenancy agreement.</p><p><strong>Redress Scheme & Client Money Protection Disclosures</strong></p><p><strong>Sterling Sales and Lettings</strong> (trading name of Sterling Property Consultants Limited) operates strictly in compliance with statutory consumer protection regulations:</p><p><strong>Redress Scheme</strong>: We are a member of the <strong>Property Redress Scheme (PRS)</strong></p><p><strong>PRS Membership Number: PRS033121</strong></p><p>This independent, government-authorised redress scheme provides consumers with free, fair, and impartial dispute resolution.</p><p><strong>Client Money Protection (CMP)</strong>: All client money held by us is protected under our membership with <strong>Client Money Protect</strong></p><p><strong>CMP Membership Number: CMP015026</strong></p><p><strong>Tenancy Deposit Protection</strong>: Security deposits taken for Assured Periodic Tenancies are registered and held securely with <strong>The Deposit Protection Service (The DPS)</strong>.</p>",
